{"verdict":"NOT_READY","summary":"The batch substantially implements S5 and all reported gates pass, but it is not ready. The S3 policy rejects the application's normal headerless presigned uploads, production can silently inherit an unapproved seven-day audio-retention policy, and required live recovery/security acceptance evidence remains pending. HEAD matches the supplied baseline, and the implementation guide is unchanged.","substeps_covered":["Prerequisites — partial: S4 provides the required private database placement, security groups, and S3 gateway endpoint wiring; S0 defines synthetic-staging defaults. Live S4 verification and production data-policy decisions remain open.","S5.1 RDS — partial: PostgreSQL 16, db.t4g.small, single-AZ staging, 50 GiB gp3, capped autoscaling, scheduled maintenance/backups, encryption, deletion protection, and final snapshots are configured. Regional class/storage availability and the selected minor version remain unverified.","S5.2 backups and recovery — partial: staging has explicit seven-day retention and production requires an explicit database-backup decision. No backup or advancing LatestRestorableTime has been observed.","S5.3 database TLS — complete in configuration: rds.force_ssl=1 is attached, existing cloud clients require verify-full with CA and hostname verification, and CA rotation is documented.","S5.4 audio bucket — incorrect: public-access blocks, owner-enforced ownership, versioning, default SSE-KMS, Bucket Keys, and TLS restrictions exist, but the encryption-header policy rejects uploads without SSE headers.","S5.5 lifecycle — complete for synthetic staging: current and noncurrent versions expire separately, multipart uploads are cleaned up, and no archive transition or Object Lock was introduced. Production retention is incorrect because unresolved policy defaults to seven days.","S5.6 overwrite race — complete as the permitted Step 9 deferral: documentation states that versioning is not immutability and requires version/checksum binding before PHI use.","S5.7 queues — complete in authored configuration: one standard queue and <name>-dlq, 300-second visibility, 20-second long polling, maxReceiveCount=3, 4/14-day retention, source-restricted redrive, SSE-KMS, and insecure-transport denial.","S5.8 key and copy boundaries — complete in design: application data uses a distinct rotating KMS key; security-log storage remains separate; documentation identifies key-loss and duplicate-copy risks. Runtime grants remain assigned to S6.","S5.9 exports — complete: no unsupported application export bucket was provisioned.","Later-step compatibility — complete at interface level: manifests expose the bucket, queue, database, and KMS identifiers needed by S6/S8/S9 without publishing credentials; restore rehearsal and audio version binding remain assigned to Step 9.","HIPAA-focused review — no authentication, session, application authorization, tenant-isolation, or audit-event code changed. The confirmed retention risk and unverified least-privilege controls are blockers below; passing tests do not establish HIPAA compliance.","Validation — fmt, clippy, test, tf-manifest, and tf-network passed as reported. Mock Terraform tests validate configuration shape but do not establish live AWS behavior."],"blockers":[{"severity":"high","file":"infra/modules/data/audio.tf:138","problem":"Confirmed availability defect: both PutObject deny statements use StringNotEqualsIfExists. For an explicit Deny using a negated IfExists operator, a missing condition key still causes the request to be denied. The application's presigner supplies Content-Type but no SSE headers, so every normal audio upload is rejected instead of receiving bucket-default SSE-KMS. The test at infra/modules/data/tests/data.tftest.hcl:115 codifies the mistaken policy shape rather than testing externally meaningful upload behavior.","required_fix":"Make each wrong-encryption denial apply only when its header is present, for example with an appropriate Null condition combined with StringNotEquals. Add behavioral evidence that a signed PUT without SSE headers succeeds while wrong-algorithm, wrong-key, unsigned GET, and insecure-transport requests fail."},{"severity":"high","file":"infra/envs/prod/foundation/variables.tf:92","problem":"Confirmed PHI retention and data-loss risk: production current and noncurrent audio retention default to the synthetic seven-day values. Production enablement validates only database backup retention and Multi-AZ, while docs/ops/deployment-contract.md:45 records production audio retention and legal-hold policy as unresolved. The example configuration can therefore be enabled and expire production audio under an unapproved policy.","required_fix":"Require explicit approved production values for current and noncurrent audio retention before enabled=true, incorporating the production legal-hold decision. Update terraform.tfvars.example and add tests proving enablement fails when either decision is omitted."},{"severity":"medium","file":"docs/ops/data-verification.md:175","problem":"S5 acceptance is unverifiable: the document states that no resources were applied and records regional RDS compatibility/minor verification, applied-resource inspection, LatestRestorableTime, upload behavior, encryption metadata, and runtime-role negative checks as pending. Thus the guide's cloud-inspection and recoverability criteria are unsatisfied despite passing offline gates.","required_fix":"After correcting the bucket policy and completing the dependent S6 roles, apply to approved synthetic staging and record the required cloud evidence: supported RDS configuration, private/encrypted resources, advancing restore time, positive and negative upload cases, object KMS metadata, queue settings, and denied runtime control mutations."},{"severity":"low","file":".agents/runs/20260918T005346.303255Z-step8-S5/00-implement.transcript.log:1","problem":"The proposed batch includes approximately 1.2 MiB of transient prompts, transcripts, duplicate gate logs, and prior review verdicts under .agents/runs. These are orchestration artifacts rather than application or operational documentation and create unnecessary repository noise and disclosure.","required_fix":"Exclude the run directory from the proposed commit and add an ignore rule if these artifacts are always local."}]}
